stance element represents standard distances between notation elements in tenths. The type attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"defines what type of distance is being defined. Valid values include hyphen (for hyphens in lyrics) and beam."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNoteSize":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The note-size type indicates the percentage of the regular note size to use for notes with a cue and large"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size as defined in the type element. The grace type is used for notes of cue size that that include a grace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. The cue type is used for all other notes with cue size, whether defined explicitly or implicitly via"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a cue element. The large type is used for notes of large size. The text content represent the numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"percentage. A value of 100 would be identical to the size of a regular note as defined by the music font."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNoteSize"}],"title":"MXLNoteSize","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNoteSize"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotesize","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteSize"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAppearance/init(lineWidth:noteSize:distance:glyph:otherAppearance:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlappearance\/init(linewidth:notesize:distance:glyph:otherappearance:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLAppearance"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"init(lineWidth:noteSize:distance:glyph:otherAppearance:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAppearance\/init(lineWidth:noteSize:distance:glyph:otherAppearance:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"lineWidth"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLineWidth","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLLineWidthV"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"noteSize"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNoteSize","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLNoteSizeV"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"distance"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLDistance","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLDistanceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"glyph"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLGlyph","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLGlyphV"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"otherAppearance"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLOtherAppearance","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLOtherAppearanceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"])"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLineWidth":{"title":"MXLLineWidth","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllinewidth","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The line-width type indicates the width of a line type in tenths. The type attribute defines what type of line"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is being defined. Values include beam, bracket, dashes, enclosure, ending, extend, heavy barline, leger, light"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"barline, octave shift, pedal, slur middle, slur tip, staff, stem, tie middle, tie tip, tuplet bracket, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wedge. The text content is expressed in tenths."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLineWidth","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLLineWidth","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineWidth"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAppearance":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAppearance","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The appearance type controls general graphical settings for the music’s final form appearance on a printed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"page of display. This includes support for line widths, definitions for note sizes, and standard distances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between notation elements, plus an extension element for other aspects of appearance."}],"title":"MXLAppearance","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAppearance","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAppearance","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlappearance"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLGlyph":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlglyph","title":"MXLGlyph","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLGlyph","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The glyph element represents what SMuFL glyph should be used for different variations of symbols that are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"semantically identical. The type attribute specifies what type of glyph is being defined. The element value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies what SMuFL glyph to use, including recommended stylistic alternates. The SMuFL glyph name should"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match the type. For instance, a type of quarter-rest would use values restQuarter, restQuarterOld, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restQuarterZ. A type of g-clef-ottava-bassa would use values gClef8vb, gClef8vbOld, or gClef8vbCClef. A type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of octave-shift-up-8 would use values ottava, ottavaBassa, ottavaBassaBa, ottavaBassaVb, or octaveBassa."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLGlyph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"}}}